## 1. 🎨 VISUAL DESIGN & UI/UX (Score: 8/10)

### 1.1 Overall Design Philosophy
AppSumo's design is **modern flat/card-based e-commerce**, similar in structural DNA to G2A or any deals marketplace, but with a distinctly **playful, mascot-driven brand layer** on top ("Sumo Dude" hero illustration, "Stay weird" tagline). Visual density is **moderate** — less crammed than a pure marketplace, with generous imagery per product card and clear section breaks ("Top 9 deals," "Just launched"). Perceived quality tier reads as **polished mid-to-premium SaaS marketplace** — closer to Product Hunt or a curated app store than a bargain-bin liquidator. Design consistency is strong: every product card (hero grid, "Top 9," "Just launched") uses an identical component (logo, name, one-line pitch, star rating, review count, price-was/price-now).

### 1.2 Color System
| Role | Color (Hex, observed/estimated) | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| Primary brand orange/yellow | Warm orange-yellow (est. `#FF7A00`–`#FFB800` range) | "Sumo" mascot branding, historically AppSumo's signature color family |
| Background (Light) | `#FFFFFF` / off-white | Main canvas |
| Text Primary | Near-black `#1A1A1A` (est.) | Headlines, product names |
